  annotation "note_1771582116432_0", anchor: "I will not speculate on what this means. I will note that no one has offered me an explanation, and that I have asked.", text: "Three departments. I asked three departments. The Custodial Office referred me to Nightshelf Cultural Liaison, who referred me to the Wake-Singer Diplomatic File, which — I am not inventing this — referred me back to the Custodial Office with a note reading 'see original filing.' The original filing says *owned_by*. A merchant guild of tunnel-dwelling penguins owns an artifact carved from the jaw of a dead orca god, currently held by orca shamans who are trying to wake that god through accumulated sacrifice. The record is perfectly clear. The record explains nothing. I have decided to find this funny.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582116432_1", anchor: "61 shards", text: "Not sixty. Sixty-one. A black market that prices to the unit rather than rounding for negotiation is not a black market. It is a treasury that declines to file paperwork.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582116432_2", anchor: "documenting a 31% extraction-output decline", text: "E'frostlings assessors profiled a covert operation's output decline to single-percentage precision. To calculate decline you need a baseline. To establish a baseline for a guild whose founding principle is that no ledger should exist, you need either a prior audit — which the Accord never sanctioned — or an informant. Thirty-one percent is too exact to be estimated and too convenient to be volunteered.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582116432_3", anchor: "fourteen crates of Class III fire-cores bearing ☽'tenebris's triple-mark arrived at Forum Floe through unregistered channels", text: "The Forum Floe, whose corruption instruments consistently register nothing. Fourteen crates of premium fire-cores arriving unregistered during a succession crisis, from an entity allied with the Exchange, to a location where nobody is measuring the right things. See my annotation on the Forum Floe's instrument calibration. The comedy writes itself.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582116432_4", anchor: "the Swaleed~ Luminary, a fire-scarred lantern whose flame authenticates the Pactum∴silenti", text: "A shadow empire built on hoarded knowledge and blood-oaths, whose entire legal architecture depends on a piece of glass not breaking. Mandatum∴absconditu teaches that power flows through hidden channels. Someone should have hidden a spare.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582116432_5", anchor: "its secrecy calcified into spite wearing the mask of devotion", text: "Alnae~ Oss said this publicly. About an allied institution. In the hearing of guilds governed by Mandatum∴absconditu — the doctrine that survival demands secrecy. The founder of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order broke the first principle of the shadow-work ethics to diagnose what was killing them. She was, of course, correct. No one who quotes this line ever notes that it violated the very thing it mourned.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
